& [Fold1Identity] preserves exact recursive public types
  + same ProcedureType and ProcedureValue identities, serde tags, fields, and variants
  + no transport replacement or semantic alias

& [Fold2Boundary] separates finite schema graph from bounded instances
  + finite canonical definition graph inside
  + arbitrary external resolution, unbounded traversal, and semantic admission outside

& [Fold3Data] makes cycles inspectable
  + recursive definition accounts, local targets, strongly connected components, counters, faults, and residuals

& [Fold4Behavior] is cycle-safe derivation
  + derive named definition once, emit local references on revisits, validate local closure, normalize without dereference, count, digest, and report residuals

& [Fold5Failure] attacks recursive amplification
  + unresolved reference, external reference, type-name collision, unstable generator name, adversarial mutual cycle, counter evasion, serde mismatch, and excessive instance depth

& [Fold6Proof] uses independent layers
  + source scan and type inventory
  + golden recursive definitions
  + graph closure and cycle tests
  + independent schema meta-validation and instance validation
  + strict serde and core semantic boundary fixtures

& [Fold7Growth] adds no runtime authority
  + profile may unlock separately signed CPMS-I02 schema work
  + it does not unlock I03 validator dependency, I04 tool definitions, provider projection, model execution, service, effect, or hardware

